T1  - Monitoring the Time-Varying Process of Infectious Disease Using an Ensemble Framework of Modified Seir Model and Machine Learning-Based Control Chart
A1  - Qu L.
A1  - Yao J.
A1  - Li L.
A1  - Li Y.
Y1  - 2025//
N2  - Infectious disease surveillance is essential for pandemic prevention, intervention, and control. Due to various factors such as changes in epidemic characteristics, government interventions, and human behavior, the spread process of infectious diseases exhibits time-varying characteristics. Existing monitoring schemes are proficient in detecting potential infections but fail to capture the dynamic nature of the epidemic evolving. To adapt to the time-varying disease spread process and provide earlier warning, an ensemble monitoring framework combining epidemiology prediction and machine learning-based statistical process control (SPC) is proposed. Specifically, based on the classic SEIR (susceptible-exposed-infectious-removed) model, a modified epidemic mathematical model is first developed to deliver predictive information. The consideration of the epidemic period-specific characteristics and temporal government policies is reflected in the classification of the population and the setting of dynamic parameters within a system of differential equations. Then, a novel control chart leveraging the techniques of support vector data description (SVDD) and real-time contrasts (RTC) is designed, which accepts both predictive and collected data in the monitoring phase. The real-world case of COVID-19 monitoring in China validated that the proposed framework can provide an 11-day advance detection and warning of pandemic spread, thereby helping to prevent outbreaks and health emergencies.Copyright © 2025, The Authors. All rights reserved.
