T1  - Development of an Accurate AI/ML-Driven COVID-19 Patient Stratification Model Predicting Disease Outcomes from Disproportionate and Scarce Clinical Datasets
A1  - Khotimchenko M.
A1  - Bundey Y.N.
A1  - Bhave R.
A1  - Baran S.W.
A1  - Chakravarty K.
A1  - Varshney J.
Y1  - 2024//
N2  - BackgroundThe COVID-19 pandemic placed an immense burden on the global healthcare system. One of the highlighted critical challenges has been the stratification of the patients to forecast disease severity and identify the most effective treatment regimens, especially in the context of the incomplete and limited nature of available patient data. To address these issues, we have developed a decision-making tool based on our artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) module, that can impute missing key clinical biomarker parameters to predict potential disease severity outcomes in patients infected with SARS-CoV-2.MethodOur novel ML-driven patient stratification module was integrated into the AI-based hybrid platform BIOiSIM, enabling accurate predictions of COVID-19 disease outcomes from incomplete clinical datasets. The model was trained and validated using publicly available clinical datasets, with a focus on patient survival outcomes. Automated statistical algorithms were deployed to select the most essential features from the input descriptors. Missing values of the patient biomarkers were filled by the multivariate imputation technique. Model stacking was employed to enhance the overall performance of the ML algorithms.ResultsThe results demonstrated that the AI/ML module can be successfully implemented to predict COVID-19 disease outcomes with an accuracy of 0.85, AUC ROC score of 0.88, and F1 Score of 0.89 u even with the datasets missing 75% of parameter values.ConclusionThese findings highlight the potential of BIOiSIM's AI/ML capabilities to support healthcare units with limited diagnostic resources by enabling personalized treatment strategies for COVID-19 patients.Copyright © 2024, The Authors. All rights reserved.
