T1  - Research on decision Support System of Medical Material Support in public health Emergencies
T3  - 2020 International Conference on Electronic Healthcare Technologies. Toronto, ON Canada.
A1  - Yin T.
A1  - Wang M.
A1  - Zhang H.
A1  - Liu W.
A1  - Xu Y.
A1  - Liu Z.
Y1  - 2020//
N2  - Background: frequent emergent public health events bring people great casualties and property losses, the outbreak of COVID -19 was a huge challenge once again to the comprehensive ability to cope with health emergency medical institutions at all levels in our country.' Quick and accurate 'emergency medical supplies is the key to win the 'battle'. Objective(s): To establish a set of intelligent decision-making system for medical material allocation in response to public health emergencies in medical institutions, so as to improve the sensitivity and accuracy of medical material emergency management by means of information, and effectively ensure a smooth and efficient epidemic prevention. Pareto analysis was used to analyze the characteristics of emergency medical supplies. Dijkstra algorithm, Floyd algorithm select the shortest path, using genetic algorithm and particle swarm optimization algorithm; to solve the problem of multi-problem stacking. The function theory method of intelligent architecture is used to analyze the scheduling and prediction of emergency materials and the uncertain factors. Result(s): As the material support management of medical institutions is an important link to control the development of the outbreak, the operation efficiency of the whole system cannot meet the current 'tight time and heavy task' epidemic prevention and control needs. There is a state of untimely deployment, unscientific deployment, asymmetric information, insufficient preparation and no priority. Therefore, a material demand model based on the priority mechanism of epidemic outbreak prevention and control is established based on the two propositions that need to be solved urgently at present. Conclusion(s): In the case of shortage of resources and many uncertain factors, the guarantee of medical supplies lacks scientific allocation decision-making principle, and the emergency guarantee of medical supplies lacks intelligent traceability management system, so as to reduce internal consumption and improve the operation efficiency of the organization.
