T1  - ECOVID-Net: an ensemble deep transfer learning based neural network for COVID-19 diagnosis using chest X-ray images.

A1  - Appasami, G.
A1  - Kavitha, Lakshmi R.
A1  - Savarimuthu, Nickolas
Y1  - 2024//
N1  - Savarimuthu, N.//
N2  - Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) is a deadly infection that affects the respiratory organs in humans. This disease turned out to be a pandemic affecting millions of individuals worldwide. Using chest radiography images is one of the critical assessment strategies for screening covid-19 cases. Due to the daily increase in cases, only a limited number of COVID-19 testing equipment are commonly available in medical centers. This article examines chest X-ray images to detect COVID-19 cases based on radiology examinations. Recently, numerous research has been done to identify COVID-19 cases using deep learning frameworks trained on X-ray images since deep learning models can extract the fine-grained features for medical image analysis. Even though some of them have achieved successful prediction, the deep learning models may be vulnerable to over-fitting, excessive variance, and lack of generalization mistakes due to noise and small datasets. Ensemble learning overcomes the limitations of deep learning by predicting outcomes with multiple models instead of one. To address this, we propose ECOVID-Net, a deep ensemble transfer learning model that incorporates both ensemble and deep learning. Finally, the explored framework is evaluated using standard performance metrics. The proposed ECOVID-Net model attains accuracy of 96.33% for four classes of classification(COVID-19, Lung Opacity, Pneumonia, Normal), 97.53% for three classes of classification (COVID-19, Pneumonia, Normal), and 98.89%, for two classes classification (COVID-19, Normal). The presented ECOVID-Net model significantly improves the existing radiology-based classification and can be a potentially beneficial tool for radiologists and clinical practitioners in diagnosing Covid-19.
