T1  - Clustering-based ensemble learning from COVID-19 respiratory sound signals for severity prediction.

A1  - Ayyavaraiah, Monelli
A1  - Venkateswarlu, Bondu
Y1  - 2024//
N1  - Ayyavaraiah, M., Venkateswarlu, B.//
N2  - Finding precise disease severity stages remains a significant challenge in the area of COVID-19 severity prediction using respiratory sound signals. The Clustering-Based Ensemble Learning from COVID-19 Respiratory Sound Signals (CELCORSS) model has been presented as a solution to this problem. With a distribution diversity approach, CELCORSS uses the acoustic and scalogram features of cough and breath sounds to select the best features. With the potential for multiple cluster membership, the framework innovates further by clustering records using these feature subsets as centroids. A weighted average approach is used to consolidate the severity predictions produced by individual classifiers trained on each cluster in ensemble learning, which increases prediction accuracy. The novel aspects of CELCORSS are its multifaceted approach to feature selection, distinctive clustering methodology, and ensemble learning, which result in a notable improvement in COVID-19 severity prediction accuracy based on respiratory sound signals.
