T1  - COVID-19 detection from x-ray images using data analytics, AIML & CNN algorithm.

A1  - Lambat, Parth
A1  - Raj, Om
Y1  - 2025//
N1  - Lambat, P., Raj, O.//
N2  - In order to manage the spread of the illness, it is crucial to have a quick detection test. COVID-19 continues to bring scary and disastrous changes to how life is handled on Earth. These can provide answers to quickly and inexpensively identifying patients with this illness. The easiest and most affordable option is the chest X-ray. In this article, we proposed a solution using a Deep Convolutional Neural Network that can identify patients who are positive for COVID-19 using chest X-ray images. We utilized several advanced CNN models in this study, such as DenseNet201, ResNet50V2, and Inceptionv3. Our models, instead of making predictions on their own, have been combined using a new method called weighted average ensemble technique. To determine how well the solution worked, we used public domain chest X-ray images from people who have COVID and people who do not have COVID. 500 pictures of COVID positive patients were divided from 500 pictures of patients who tested negative for the virus. The pictures of COVID positive patients were then assigned to the training, testing, and validation sets. The suggested method has achieved a classification accuracy of 91.62%, which is higher than the latest CNN models in comparison to the benchmark algorithm; the suggested technique achieved a classification accuracy of 91%. Any doctor can use this program on any computer to quickly identify COVID-positive patients using chest X-ray images. RTPCR are strongly sensitive and accurate, but many times are expensive and unavailable in rural places. X-Ray are available in Macro and Micro-rural places, that makes it accessible and if combined with our AIML & CNN Algorithm and would be a much quicker and more affordable than PCR tests.
