T1  - Projected baselines of COVID-19 in the EU/EEA and the UK for assessing the impact of de-escalation of measures.


Y1  - 2020//
N2  - This article aims to provide a short-term 30-day forecast of the expected number of COVID-19 cases, deaths and hospitalized cases (including general hospital ward and intensive care unit) under a set of assumptions. An assessment of the risk associated with the COVID-19 epidemic and the response strategies applied or envisaged should be based on a comprehensive analysis taking in consideration current uncertainties, the specific epidemiological situation in each country, and outputs of models according to new scientific evidences. Future work in this area intends to promote data sharing and operational forecasting through an "ensemble modelling" approach. This approach combines predictions from different mathematical models to improve on a single-model forecast, offering more accurate predictions of epidemic trends and clarifying the uncertainties associated with these predictions.
