T1  - Synthesis, molecular docking, and binding Gibbs free energy calculation of beta-nitrostyrene derivatives: Potential inhibitors of SARS-CoV-2 3CL protease.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.molstruc.2023.135409
A1  - Jia, Ze-Jun
A1  - Lan, Xiao-Wei
A1  - Lu, Kui
A1  - Meng, Xuan
A1  - Jing, Wen-Jie
A1  - Jia, Shi-Ru
A1  - Zhao, Kai
A1  - Dai, Yu-Jie
Y1  - 2023//
Y2  - 20230323//
N2  - The outbreak of novel coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19), caused by the novel coronavirus (SARS-CoV-2), has had a significant impact on human health and the economic development. SARS-CoV-2 3CL protease (3CLpro) is highly conserved and plays a key role in mediating the transcription of virus replication. It is an ideal target for the design and screening of anti-coronavirus drugs. In this work, seven beta-nitrostyrene derivatives were synthesized by Henry reaction and beta-dehydration reaction, and their inhibitory effects on SARS-CoV-2 3CL protease were identified by enzyme activity inhibition assay in vitro. Among them, 4-nitro-beta-nitrostyrene (compound a) showed the lowest IC50 values of 0.7297 microM. To investigate the key groups that determine the activity of beta-nitrostyrene derivatives and their interaction mode with the receptor, the molecular docking using the CDOCKER protocol in Discovery Studio 2016 was performed. The results showed that the hydrogen bonds between beta-NO2 and receptor GLY-143 and the pi-pi stacking between the aryl ring of the ligand and the imidazole ring of receptor HIS-41 significantly contributed to the ligand activity. Furthermore, the ligand-receptor absolute binding Gibbs free energies were calculated using the Binding Affinity Tool (BAT.py) to verify its correlation with the activity of beta-nitrostyrene 3CLpro inhibitors as a scoring function. The higher correlation(r2=0.6) indicates that the absolute binding Gibbs free energy based on molecular dynamics can be used to predict the activity of new beta-nitrostyrene 3CLpro inhibitors. These results provide valuable insights for the functional group-based design, structure optimization and the discovery of high accuracy activity prediction means of anti-COVID-19 lead compounds. Copyright © 2023 Published by Elsevier B.V.
