A1  - Huang, Haijun
Y1  - 2022//
Y2  - 20221101//
N2  - Background: Persistence of long-term COVID-19 pandemic is putting high pressure on healthcare services worldwide for several years. This article aims to establish models to predict infection levels and mortality of COVID-19 patients in China., Methods: Machine learning models and deep learning models have been built based on the clinical features of COVID-19 patients. The best models are selected by area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUC) scores to construct two homogeneous ensemble models for predicting infection levels and mortality, respectively. The first-hand clinical data of 760 patients are collected from Zhongnan Hospital of Wuhan University between 3 January and 8 March 2020. We preprocess data with cleaning, imputation, and normalization., Results: Our models obtain AUC = 0.7059 and Recall (Weighted avg) = 0.7248 in predicting infection level, while AUC=0.8436 and Recall (Weighted avg) = 0.8486 in predicting mortality ratio. This study also identifies two sets of essential clinical features. One is C-reactive protein (CRP) or high sensitivity C-reactive protein (hs-CRP) and the other is chest tightness, age, and pleural effusion., Conclusions: Two homogeneous ensemble models are proposed to predict infection levels and mortality of COVID-19 patients in China. New findings of clinical features for benefiting the machine learning models are reported. The evaluation of an actual dataset collected from January 3 to March 8, 2020 demonstrates the effectiveness of the models by comparing them with state-of-the-art models in prediction. Copyright © The Author(s) 2022.
